    "result_text": "The full suite passes (279 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner when their city already contains 8 owners, responding with **400**.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RejectOverCityCap.java`:\n- Counts existing owners in the same city (matched case-insensitively and ignoring surrounding/repeated whitespace, reusing the existing `OwnerFieldNormalizer`), excluding the owner being created.\n- Throws the checked `BadRequestException` (already wired to a 400 escalation handler) when the count reaches the cap of 8.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted a `rejectOverCityCap` step in the pipeline right after `normalizeCity` (so the city is already normalized) and before `rejectDuplicate`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 added two cases to `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`:\n- 9th create into a city that already has 8 owners \u2192 400.\n- Create into a city with 7 owners \u2192 201, confirming the boundary allows below the cap.\n\nThe count uses normalized city comparison, consistent with the sibling `NormalizeOwnerCity`/`RejectDuplicateOwner` functions, so cities differing only in case/whitespace count as the same.",
